    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d0bc8cd0_7095698e",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/wifi_legacy_hal.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 547,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-11-18T01:38:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s unfortunate that the API was specified as non-const. But given that\u0027s what we have to work with, I think we\u0027re better off copying the const-arg into a (non-const) local, and using that local for the arg to the vendor HAL.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 547,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 547,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "705baa8ddabb43bd6800794b5b7e994607eb8125",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d0bc8cd0_ab75cf3b",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/wifi_legacy_hal.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 547,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-11-18T17:27:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Even if we copy the \"const std::string\" to a local \"std::string\", std::string.c_str() will always return \"const char *\". So, we\u0027ll need the cast even then.",
      "parentUuid": "d0bc8cd0_7095698e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 547,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 547,
        "endChar": 23
      },
